## Program Leader

### Connor Miller

**Connor** is an operations leader and entrepreneur who combines a background in business management with a deep passion for youth and young adult discipleship. After beginning his B.A in Mechanical Engineering, he changed gears and graduated from Bethel University in 2016 with a B.A. in Business Administration and minor in Marketing. Desiring to avoid financial debt and nurture his desire to create, he funded his education by co-founding two small businesses and scaling the property management division during high school and college years. He expressed his love for problem solving through participating in high school robotics and eventually interned at a robotic automation company where he would troubleshoot and reprogram systems. To continue his passion for problem solving, he mentored his high school robotics team while studying his bachelor's degree and growing his businesses.&nbsp;

Eventually, Connor discovered a genuine love for camping ministry while serving as a camp counselor for two summers. In 2018 he sold his business assets and joined full time at Bear Lake Camp in Albion, Indiana, as Business Manager, a role he held through 2025. In 2020, he also stepped into the role of Director of Operations at Camp Otyokwah, where he has helped oversee the logistics, systems, and day-to-day operations of both ministries. In 2026 he became the **Site Director** at Otyokwah.

Throughout his career, Connor has developed a strong desire to use problem-solving, organization, and thoughtful decision-making to help create environments where young people can grow in their faith. He believes that both small and large decisions should be approached with intentionality, discernment, and a desire to honor Christ. Rather than simply solving problems for the sake of efficiency, Connor is passionate about using these skills to build healthy environments and ultimately help young people walk faithfully with Jesus.

Driven by a desire to see young adults become more like Christ, Connor seeks to bring together practical leadership and intentional discipleship. His goal is to help cultivate environments where young people can discover their identity in Christ, develop healthy boundaries, make wise decisions, and learn what it looks like to faithfully live out their faith in everyday life.

**Contact email: [connor@otyokwah.org](mailto:connor@otyokwah.org)**

