## Discipleship Leader

### Evan Fairrow

**Evan** has a deep passion for youth discipleship, meaningful relationships, and helping young people discover what it means to faithfully follow Christ. He is passionate about walking alongside students through the questions, challenges, and decisions that shape their lives while creating environments where they can be known, challenged, and equipped to grow in their faith.

Evan graduated from Miami University with a B.A. in Psychology and a minor in Childhood Studies before earning his M.A. in Clinical Mental Health Counseling from The Ohio State University. He is a Licensed Professional Counselor and seeks to thoughtfully combine biblical truth, relational ministry, and applicable clinical skills to better understand and serve young people. He is particularly passionate about helping students develop healthy identities, relationships, boundaries, and patterns of living that are grounded in Christ.

Evan has been involved with Camp Otyokwah for six years. After serving as a camp counselor for two summers, he joined the full-time staff as Program Director in 2023, helping lead and coordinate summer programming alongside the resident staff team. He now serves as Camp Otyokwah’s **Discipleship Director**, focusing on creating meaningful opportunities for spiritual growth and helping cultivate a culture centered on knowing and following Christ.

Throughout school, Evan was heavily involved with Cru, where he led Bible studies, discipled students, spoke publicly, coordinated outreach initiatives, and helped shape organizational vision. These experiences deepened his desire to invest in the lives of young people and help them develop a faith that extends beyond church and into everyday life.

Evan has a great desire to see young people become genuine disciples of Jesus—people whose identity is rooted in Christ and whose faith shapes how they think, make decisions, navigate relationships, and live their lives as a reflection of Jesus in the world.

**Contact email: [evan@otyokwah.org](mailto:evan@otyokwah.org)**

